+# Talking-head ready-session callback owner — local implementation
+
+Production construction now uses `ReadySessionOwner` and `ReadyAvatarAdapter`.
+It preserves the classic **audio AND video** profile. `handler.ts` connects the
+npm BYOR callback to the owner's private Unix socket; no HTTP receiver or Chert
+protocol implementation is required in application code. The deployed receiver
+and remote worker are unchanged; this directory has not been deployed.
+
+## Preparation and admission
+
+Start/check/health never warm, create, dispatch, refill, or start an agent. Incoming
+callbacks ONLY claim an already-ready session; they never invoke provider
+preparation. The application/operator explicitly stages a slot through the
+separate admin socket (`control.py ... stage SLOT_ID`). This is a potentially paid
+application operation and must not be wired into connector startup or health.
+No staging command was run against real services during implementation.
+
+Staging uses the existing 45-second preparation budget, exact existing demo dispatch
+format and classic profile. The existing AvatarAdapter verifies the intended
+participant's audio and video publications and heartbeat. Incoming claims retain
+the original four-second callback deadline. Audio-only requests decline explicitly;
+video is never silently disabled. The CLI and central BYOR mode must include the
+new mode-aware video change before deployment. Signaling compatibility does not
+prove decoded or end-to-end FaceTime video.
+
+The owner holds one slot. An atomic fsynced record binds a ready slot to one exact
+operation/call digest before releasing credentials. Duplicates return the same
+in-memory decision; conflicts and a second call cannot steal the session. Claims
+never extend agent/token expiry or silently truncate the configured conversation.
+The 600-second call policy is retained. Unclaimed slots expire using the same
+bounded idle-window calculation as ContinuousDemo. After verified cleanup, the
+application may explicitly stage another slot. Automatic continuous refill is
+not enabled: the old HTTP warm watcher is not imported or run.
+
+## Durable ownership and cleanup
+
+Use fresh journals and drain the old receiver before changing owners. An existing
+process-local Railway warm slot cannot be imported or stolen. There is one owner
+for preparation, claims, expiry and cleanup; Node owns no LiveKit effects.
+`ready_owner.py` uses a distinct journal fingerprint and rejects the old callback
+journal. Never copy, overwrite or remove historical resource receipts to migrate.
+
+Room intent and an ownership marker are saved before create. The returned room
+SID is persisted before dispatch. Cleanup checks the exact SID and marker, then
+uses existing AvatarAdapter cleanup/absence and owned rendering-room checks.
+A foreign replacement, unavailable API or failed verification retains debt.
+A completed preparation is settled. Timeout, SDK cancellation or process death
+while staging stays uncertain even when inventory is empty; there is no blind
+redispatch or guessed settlement. Admin `status` exposes that state; no force-clean
+or reset command exists. External authoritative settlement evidence remains an
+operator gate for those rare interrupted operations.
+
+Lifecycle acknowledgments persist separately from cleanup. The owner runs its
+own maintenance loop, independent of Node: terminal cancellation and bounded call
+expiry drive cleanup and retry. Accepted calls survive process restart until their
+saved terminal/expiry; shutdown does not delete them. Ready slots reopen unavailable
+until the original room's ownership/media are refreshed without allocation. No
+bearer tokens are stored in either application journal.
+
+## Process and storage arrangement
+
+`server.py --initialize-state` creates fresh journals only and refuses existing
+state. Run this explicit local setup once, after selecting a durable mount. Normal
+server startup requires both journals to exist; a missing mount cannot silently
+become a new empty owner. Never use initialization as a recovery operation.
+
+`server.py` runs only the application owner and IPC/maintenance. The existing remote
+agent continues under its own supervisor. Python needs application provider
+credentials; Node needs only Chert credentials and `TALKING_HEAD_CALLBACK_SOCKET`.
+Use separate environment files and explicit immutable release paths.
+
+Required absolute paths:
+
+- `CHERT_JOURNAL_PATH`: existing application resource receipts, in a fresh directory.
+- `TALKING_HEAD_OPERATION_JOURNAL`: durable ready-slot/claim journal.
+- `TALKING_HEAD_CALLBACK_SOCKET`: private callback-only endpoint.
+- `TALKING_HEAD_ADMIN_SOCKET`: separate explicit staging/cancel/status endpoint.
+
+Existing Config environment names still apply, including unused webhook route
+configuration (no HTTP server is started), namespace and token/resource TTLs. The
+classic continuous profile requires token TTL greater than resource TTL plus 60s.
+Use a private POSIX local persistent filesystem, 0700 directories/0600 files,
+single writer, and the receiver's pinned Python dependencies. Do not use ephemeral
+container state or a shared multi-host filesystem. There is no mandatory Docker.
+
+The journals use kernel writer locks; socket leases permit safe stale-socket
+recovery after process death and refuse symlinks/foreign files. Never remove a
+live writer's locks. The Node journal deliberately still requires reviewed
+recovery after SIGKILL leaves its crash lock; a normal stop/restart releases it.
+Application expiry continues even while Node is blocked on that recovery.
+
+Local subprocess tests qualify owner SIGKILL/reopen, writer exclusion, private
+storage, terminal cleanup and independent expiry. They do **not** qualify Railway
+volume mounting or a Linux systemd installation. Reviewed example units are in `connector/host/`; the CLI results record
+the remaining host gate.
+No remote host was accessed or changed. Before activation, verify the selected
+host's mount persistence, process supervision and restart recovery with fresh
+state and explicit old-owner drain.
+
+## Tests and historical prototype
+
+`tests/test_ready_owner.py`, `test_host.py`, and the installed npm package test use
+production construction/media policy with only provider transports substituted.
+Both publications are required, with no synthetic audio policy. Acceptance,
+claims, restart and cleanup are exercised without a real agent/provider session.
+The earlier `owner.py` cold-preparation prototype and its audio-policy fixture
+remain for regression/history only; production `server.py` no longer constructs it.
+See `chert-facetime-cli/docs/talking-head-compatibility/RESULTS.md` for evidence.
